1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,331
Welcome to Unit Two of Algebra One, where
we start solving equations.

2
00:00:04,781 --> 00:00:09,200
In this lesson, we'll solve one-step
equations, and learn the one rule that

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,733
makes every equation work.

4
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:16,539
An equation says two things are equal. You
can picture it as a balanced scale.

5
00:00:16,989 --> 00:00:20,338
Here, x plus three on the left balances
seven on the right.

6
00:00:20,788 --> 00:00:25,889
If you take three away from the left side
only, the scale tips. To keep it balanced,

7
00:00:25,889 --> 00:00:28,319
take three away from the right side too.

8
00:00:28,769 --> 00:00:33,234
That's the golden rule of equations:
whatever you do to one side, do to the

9
00:00:33,234 --> 00:00:33,889
other side.

10
00:00:35,033 --> 00:00:40,637
To solve, we want x alone on one side. We
undo whatever is being done to x, using

11
00:00:40,637 --> 00:00:42,159
the inverse operation.

12
00:00:42,609 --> 00:00:47,684
Addition and subtraction undo each other.
Multiplication and division undo each

13
00:00:47,684 --> 00:00:48,070
other.

14
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:54,161
In x plus three equals seven, three is
added to x. So we subtract three from both

15
00:00:54,161 --> 00:00:54,579
sides.

16
00:00:55,029 --> 00:01:00,542
x plus three minus three is just x, and
seven minus three is four. So x equals

17
00:01:00,542 --> 00:01:00,895
four.

18
00:01:02,033 --> 00:01:05,959
Always check your answer by putting it
back into the original equation.

19
00:01:06,409 --> 00:01:11,337
Four plus three is seven. Seven equals
seven, so x equals four is correct.

20
00:01:12,467 --> 00:01:18,330
Now x minus five equals two. Five is
subtracted from x, so we add five to both

21
00:01:18,330 --> 00:01:18,781
sides.

22
00:01:19,231 --> 00:01:24,735
x minus five plus five is x, and two plus
five is seven. So x equals seven.

23
00:01:25,867 --> 00:01:31,404
Next, four x equals twenty. Here x is
multiplied by four, so we divide both

24
00:01:31,404 --> 00:01:32,437
sides by four.

25
00:01:32,887 --> 00:01:39,351
Four x divided by four is x, and twenty
divided by four is five. So x equals five.

26
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:46,956
Finally, x divided by three equals six. x
is divided by three, so we multiply both

27
00:01:46,956 --> 00:01:48,137
sides by three.

28
00:01:48,587 --> 00:01:54,433
x over three, times three, is x. Six times
three is eighteen. So x equals eighteen.

29
00:01:54,883 --> 00:01:57,656
Check: eighteen divided by three is six.
It works.

30
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:01,808
Your turn. Solve negative three x equals
twelve.

31
00:02:02,258 --> 00:02:03,709
Pause the video and try it.

32
00:02:04,159 --> 00:02:09,407
x is multiplied by negative three, so
divide both sides by negative three.

33
00:02:09,857 --> 00:02:15,254
Twelve divided by negative three is
negative four. So x equals negative four.

34
00:02:15,704 --> 00:02:19,331
Check: negative three times negative four
is twelve. Correct.

35
00:02:20,466 --> 00:02:24,477
Let's work through one-step equations that
use fractions and decimals.

36
00:02:25,899 --> 00:02:31,606
Solve two one-step equations. First,
negative two thirds x equals fourteen.

37
00:02:31,606 --> 00:02:36,779
Second, y minus four point seven five
equals negative one point two.

38
00:02:37,899 --> 00:02:43,825
In the first equation, x is multiplied by
negative two thirds. To undo it, multiply

39
00:02:43,825 --> 00:02:45,110
by the reciprocal.

40
00:02:46,233 --> 00:02:51,595
Multiply both sides by negative three
halves. On the left, the fractions cancel

41
00:02:51,595 --> 00:02:52,206
to one x.

42
00:02:53,333 --> 00:02:57,770
On the right, fourteen times negative
three halves is negative twenty one.

43
00:02:58,899 --> 00:03:04,476
In the second equation, four point seven
five is subtracted from y, so add four

44
00:03:04,476 --> 00:03:06,665
point seven five to both sides.

45
00:03:07,799 --> 00:03:12,983
Negative one point two plus four point
seven five is three point five five.

46
00:03:14,133 --> 00:03:18,250
So x is negative twenty one and y is three
point five five.

47
00:03:19,399 --> 00:03:24,241
Watch out. When x is multiplied by a
fraction, multiply by its reciprocal

48
00:03:24,241 --> 00:03:29,414
instead of dividing. Keep the negative
sign with it. And check by substituting

49
00:03:29,414 --> 00:03:29,746
back.

50
00:03:30,866 --> 00:03:36,546
Your turn. Solve five fourths n equals
negative thirty five, and k plus two point

51
00:03:36,546 --> 00:03:40,402
six equals zero point nine. Pause the
video and try it.

52
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:50,802
Multiply by four fifths to get n equals
negative twenty eight. Subtract two point

53
00:03:50,802 --> 00:03:54,063
six to get k equals negative one point
seven.

54
00:03:55,200 --> 00:04:00,235
Some equations need two steps to solve,
like three x plus five equals twenty.

55
00:04:00,685 --> 00:04:03,842
In this lesson, we'll learn which step to
do first, and why.

56
00:04:04,967 --> 00:04:10,172
To build three x plus five, you start with
x, multiply by three, then add five.

57
00:04:10,622 --> 00:04:15,866
To solve, we undo those steps in reverse
order. First undo the adding, then undo

58
00:04:15,866 --> 00:04:16,915
the multiplying.

59
00:04:17,365 --> 00:04:21,767
It's like getting dressed. You put on
socks, then shoes. To undress, the shoes

60
00:04:21,767 --> 00:04:22,613
come off first.

61
00:04:23,733 --> 00:04:26,443
Let's solve three x plus five equals
twenty.

62
00:04:26,893 --> 00:04:31,458
First, subtract five from both sides. That
gives three x equals fifteen.

63
00:04:31,908 --> 00:04:35,193
Then divide both sides by three. x equals
five.

64
00:04:35,643 --> 00:04:38,886
Check: three times five, plus five, is
twenty. It works.

65
00:04:40,033 --> 00:04:42,721
Next, x over four, minus two, equals
three.

66
00:04:43,171 --> 00:04:46,947
First add two to both sides, so x over
four equals five.

67
00:04:47,397 --> 00:04:50,917
Then multiply both sides by four. x equals
twenty.

68
00:04:52,067 --> 00:04:55,501
Watch the signs in seven minus two x
equals fifteen.

69
00:04:55,951 --> 00:05:00,495
Subtract seven from both sides. That
leaves negative two x equals eight.

70
00:05:00,945 --> 00:05:05,297
Divide both sides by negative two, and x
equals negative four.

71
00:05:05,747 --> 00:05:10,675
Check: seven minus two times negative four
is seven plus eight, which is fifteen.

72
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:16,794
One exception. In the quantity x plus
four, all over three, equals five, the

73
00:05:16,794 --> 00:05:19,160
whole left side is divided by three.

74
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:24,770
So this time we multiply both sides by
three first, to get x plus four equals

75
00:05:24,770 --> 00:05:25,306
fifteen.

76
00:05:25,756 --> 00:05:28,316
Then subtract four, and x equals eleven.

77
00:05:29,433 --> 00:05:32,932
Your turn. Solve five x minus eight equals
seventeen.

78
00:05:33,382 --> 00:05:34,833
Pause the video and try it.

79
00:05:35,283 --> 00:05:38,653
Add eight to both sides, so five x equals
twenty-five.

80
00:05:39,103 --> 00:05:42,282
Divide both sides by five, and x equals
five.

81
00:05:42,732 --> 00:05:46,273
Check: five times five minus eight is
seventeen. Correct.

82
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:51,539
Here's a worked two-step equation where
the variable is part of a fraction.

83
00:05:52,967 --> 00:05:57,852
Solve the quantity three x minus four, all
over five, equals negative two.

84
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:05,058
The whole numerator is divided by five, so
undo that first by multiplying both sides

85
00:06:05,058 --> 00:06:05,635
by five.

86
00:06:06,767 --> 00:06:10,863
That clears the fraction: three x minus
four equals negative ten.

87
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,328
Add four to both sides. Three x equals
negative six.

88
00:06:16,467 --> 00:06:19,368
Divide by three, and x equals negative
two.

89
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:23,017
The solution is x equals negative two.

90
00:06:24,167 --> 00:06:29,078
Watch out. The fraction bar acts like
parentheses, so the whole numerator is

91
00:06:29,078 --> 00:06:34,053
divided by five. Undo the last operation
first, which here is the division. A

92
00:06:34,053 --> 00:06:37,543
common mistake is dividing only part of
the numerator.

93
00:06:38,667 --> 00:06:43,879
Your turn. Solve the quantity two x plus
seven, over three, equals five. Pause the

94
00:06:43,879 --> 00:06:44,960
video and try it.

95
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:55,929
Multiply by three: two x plus seven equals
fifteen. Subtract seven and divide by two:

96
00:06:55,929 --> 00:06:56,988
x equals four.

97
00:06:58,133 --> 00:07:02,656
Real equations often take several steps,
and can have x on both sides.

98
00:07:03,106 --> 00:07:06,476
In this lesson, we'll use a simple plan
that solves them all.

99
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:10,949
Here's the plan. First, distribute to
clear any parentheses.

100
00:07:11,399 --> 00:07:13,618
Second, combine like terms on each side.

101
00:07:14,068 --> 00:07:18,228
Third, if x appears on both sides, move
the x terms to one side.

102
00:07:18,678 --> 00:07:23,946
Then finish like a two-step equation: undo
adding or subtracting, then undo

103
00:07:23,946 --> 00:07:25,632
multiplying or dividing.

104
00:07:26,766 --> 00:07:31,566
Let's solve two times the quantity x plus
three, plus four, equals eighteen.

105
00:07:32,016 --> 00:07:35,984
Distribute the two: two x plus six, plus
four, equals eighteen.

106
00:07:36,434 --> 00:07:39,613
Combine like terms: two x plus ten equals
eighteen.

107
00:07:40,063 --> 00:07:45,922
Subtract ten from both sides, to get two x
equals eight. Divide by two, and x equals

108
00:07:45,922 --> 00:07:46,271
four.

109
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:51,304
Next, five x minus two plus three x equals
forty-six.

110
00:07:51,754 --> 00:07:56,618
Combine five x and three x, to get eight x
minus two equals forty-six.

111
00:07:57,068 --> 00:08:01,569
Add two to both sides: eight x equals
forty-eight. So x equals six.

112
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:07,628
Now x is on both sides: five x plus three
equals two x plus eighteen.

113
00:08:08,078 --> 00:08:13,510
Subtract two x from both sides, so the x
terms are together on the left. That gives

114
00:08:13,510 --> 00:08:15,800
three x plus three equals eighteen.

115
00:08:16,250 --> 00:08:21,264
Subtract three: three x equals fifteen.
Divide by three: x equals five.

116
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:27,157
A useful tip: move the smaller x term, so
you avoid a negative coefficient.

117
00:08:27,607 --> 00:08:33,410
In four x minus seven equals nine x plus
eight, subtract four x from both sides.

118
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:36,910
That gives negative seven equals five x
plus eight.

119
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:42,480
Subtract eight: negative fifteen equals
five x. So x equals negative three.

120
00:08:42,930 --> 00:08:45,640
Check: both sides come out to negative
nineteen.

121
00:08:46,766 --> 00:08:52,272
Let's use the whole plan on three times
the quantity x minus four, equals x plus

122
00:08:52,272 --> 00:08:52,548
six.

123
00:08:52,998 --> 00:08:56,432
Distribute: three x minus twelve equals x
plus six.

124
00:08:56,882 --> 00:09:00,914
Subtract x from both sides: two x minus
twelve equals six.

125
00:09:01,364 --> 00:09:04,863
Add twelve: two x equals eighteen. So x
equals nine.

126
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:11,059
Your turn. Solve two times the quantity
three x plus one, equals four x plus

127
00:09:11,059 --> 00:09:11,525
twelve.

128
00:09:11,975 --> 00:09:13,426
Pause the video and try it.

129
00:09:13,876 --> 00:09:17,524
Distribute: six x plus two equals four x
plus twelve.

130
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:23,968
Subtract four x: two x plus two equals
twelve. Subtract two: two x equals ten.

131
00:09:24,418 --> 00:09:28,045
So x equals five. Check: both sides equal
thirty-two.

132
00:09:29,166 --> 00:09:34,286
Now a full multi-step equation, with
parentheses and variables on both sides.

133
00:09:35,733 --> 00:09:41,287
Solve four times the quantity two x minus
three, minus x, equals three times the

134
00:09:41,287 --> 00:09:43,370
quantity x plus two, plus two.

135
00:09:44,499 --> 00:09:50,905
Distribute on both sides. Four times two x
minus three is eight x minus twelve. Three

136
00:09:50,905 --> 00:09:53,694
times x plus two is three x plus six.

137
00:09:54,833 --> 00:10:00,429
Combine like terms on each side. Eight x
minus x is seven x, and six plus two is

138
00:10:00,429 --> 00:10:00,849
eight.

139
00:10:01,966 --> 00:10:07,785
Move the smaller x term. Subtract three x
from both sides to get four x minus twelve

140
00:10:07,785 --> 00:10:08,686
equals eight.

141
00:10:09,833 --> 00:10:12,905
Add twelve to both sides. Four x equals
twenty.

142
00:10:14,033 --> 00:10:16,251
Divide by four. x equals five.

143
00:10:17,399 --> 00:10:19,341
The solution is x equals five.

144
00:10:21,399 --> 00:10:26,667
Watch out. Simplify each side completely
before you move anything across. Move the

145
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:31,614
smaller x term to keep the coefficient
positive. And check by evaluating each

146
00:10:31,614 --> 00:10:32,642
side separately.

147
00:10:33,766 --> 00:10:39,795
Your turn. Solve five times x minus one,
plus two x, equals two times x plus four,

148
00:10:39,795 --> 00:10:42,662
plus seven. Pause the video and try it.

149
00:10:47,199 --> 00:10:54,006
Simplify to seven x minus five equals two
x plus fifteen. Subtract two x, add five:

150
00:10:54,006 --> 00:10:57,205
five x equals twenty, so x equals four.

151
00:10:58,333 --> 00:11:03,492
Most equations have exactly one solution.
But some have none at all, and some have

152
00:11:03,492 --> 00:11:04,498
infinitely many.

153
00:11:04,948 --> 00:11:07,658
In this lesson, we'll learn how to tell
which is which.

154
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:12,170
First, the usual case. Two x plus one
equals seven.

155
00:11:12,620 --> 00:11:17,915
Subtract one, then divide by two, and x
equals three. Exactly one number works.

156
00:11:17,915 --> 00:11:19,255
That's one solution.

157
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:23,941
Now try three x plus five equals three x
minus two.

158
00:11:24,391 --> 00:11:29,621
Subtract three x from both sides. The x
terms cancel, and we're left with five

159
00:11:29,621 --> 00:11:30,962
equals negative two.

160
00:11:31,412 --> 00:11:36,885
That's false. Five never equals negative
two, no matter what x is. So this equation

161
00:11:36,885 --> 00:11:37,940
has no solution.

162
00:11:38,390 --> 00:11:42,865
On a graph, the two sides are parallel
lines. They have the same slope, so they

163
00:11:42,865 --> 00:11:43,488
never meet.

164
00:11:44,633 --> 00:11:48,942
Next, two times the quantity x plus three,
equals two x plus six.

165
00:11:49,392 --> 00:11:52,827
Distribute: two x plus six equals two x
plus six.

166
00:11:53,277 --> 00:11:58,418
Subtract two x from both sides, and we get
six equals six. That's always true.

167
00:11:58,868 --> 00:12:03,684
Every value of x works, so there are
infinitely many solutions. The two sides

168
00:12:03,684 --> 00:12:05,247
are really the same line.

169
00:12:06,366 --> 00:12:10,889
Here's the rule. Simplify until the x
terms are gone, or you have x alone.

170
00:12:11,339 --> 00:12:13,302
If x is left, there's one solution.

171
00:12:13,752 --> 00:12:17,464
If x disappears and the statement is
false, there's no solution.

172
00:12:17,914 --> 00:12:23,115
If x disappears and the statement is true,
there are infinitely many solutions, all

173
00:12:23,115 --> 00:12:23,930
real numbers.

174
00:12:25,066 --> 00:12:30,332
Let's try one more. Five times the
quantity x minus one, equals five x plus

175
00:12:30,332 --> 00:12:30,613
one.

176
00:12:31,063 --> 00:12:34,924
Distribute: five x minus five equals five
x plus one.

177
00:12:35,374 --> 00:12:40,537
Subtract five x: negative five equals one.
That's false, so there's no solution.

178
00:12:41,666 --> 00:12:46,829
Your turn. Solve three times the quantity
x plus two, equals three x plus six.

179
00:12:47,279 --> 00:12:48,730
Pause the video and try it.

180
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:52,742
Distribute: three x plus six equals three
x plus six.

181
00:12:53,192 --> 00:12:57,992
Subtract three x: six equals six. That's
true, so there are infinitely many

182
00:12:57,992 --> 00:12:58,632
solutions.

183
00:12:59,766 --> 00:13:03,649
Let's decide how many solutions an
equation has, step by step.

184
00:13:05,066 --> 00:13:10,979
How many solutions does each equation
have? First, six times x minus two equals

185
00:13:10,979 --> 00:13:17,116
two times three x plus one. Second, four x
minus two times x minus five equals two

186
00:13:17,116 --> 00:13:18,463
times x plus five.

187
00:13:19,599 --> 00:13:24,954
In the first equation, distribute: six x
minus twelve equals six x plus two.

188
00:13:26,099 --> 00:13:31,379
Subtract six x from both sides. The x
terms disappear and we get negative twelve

189
00:13:31,379 --> 00:13:33,161
equals two, which is false.

190
00:13:34,299 --> 00:13:40,156
In the second equation, distribute the
negative two: four x minus two x plus ten

191
00:13:40,156 --> 00:13:41,766
equals two x plus ten.

192
00:13:42,899 --> 00:13:46,163
Combine like terms. Both sides are two x
plus ten.

193
00:13:47,299 --> 00:13:51,246
Subtract two x, and we get ten equals ten,
which is always true.

194
00:13:52,366 --> 00:13:57,669
Equation a has no solution, because it
simplifies to a false statement. Equation

195
00:13:57,669 --> 00:14:03,104
b has infinitely many solutions, because
both sides are identical, so every number

196
00:14:03,104 --> 00:14:03,502
works.

197
00:14:04,633 --> 00:14:09,405
Watch out. A false statement means no
solution. It does not mean x equals zero.

198
00:14:09,405 --> 00:14:13,936
A true statement means every number is a
solution. And distribute negatives

199
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:16,473
carefully, or you will get the wrong case.

200
00:14:17,599 --> 00:14:23,182
Your turn. How many solutions do three
times two x plus four equals six x plus

201
00:14:23,182 --> 00:14:28,908
twelve, and five x minus one equals five
times x plus one, have? Pause the video

202
00:14:28,908 --> 00:14:29,695
and try it.

203
00:14:34,233 --> 00:14:39,610
The first gives six x plus twelve on both
sides, so infinitely many. The second

204
00:14:39,610 --> 00:14:42,809
gives negative one equals five, so no
solution.

205
00:14:43,933 --> 00:14:49,162
Next up: Literal Equations and Formulas.
If this helped, subscribe to School STEM,

206
00:14:49,162 --> 00:14:49,799
Explained.

